1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:07,340
(Sheldon:)Worst Renaissance fair ever.

2
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,305
(Leonard:)Please let it go, Sheldon.

3
00:00:10,468 --> 00:00:13,508
SHELDON:
It was rife with historical inaccuracies.

4
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,180
(Sheldon:)For example, the tavern girl
serving flagons of mead.

5
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,639
(Sheldon:)Now, her costume
was obviously Germanic...

6
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:23,020
(Sheldon:)...but in 1487, the Bavarian purity laws,
or Reinheitsgebot...

7
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:25,609
(Sheldon:)...severely limited the availability
of mead.

8
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:27,775
(Sheldon:)At best,
they would've had some spiced wine.

9
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:30,534
LEONARD: You're nitpicking.
SHELDON: Oh, really?

10
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,237
(Sheldon:)Well, here's another nit for you.

11
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:35,537
(Sheldon:)The flagons would not have been made
of polypropylene.

12
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:38,742
(Howard:)Renaissance fairs
aren't about historical accuracy.

13
00:00:38,913 --> 00:00:41,503
(Howard:)They're about taking chubby girls
who work at Kinko's...

14
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,666
(Howard:)...and lacing them up
in corsets so tight...

15
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:46,795
(Howard:)...their bosom jumps out
and says, "Howdy."

16
00:00:47,589 --> 00:00:50,219
Bosoms would not have said, "Howdy,"
in the 15th century.

17
00:00:50,383 --> 00:00:52,633
(Sheldon:)If anything,
they would've said, "Huzzah."

18
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,802
(Howard:)I don't care what the bosoms say,
Sheldon.

19
00:00:54,971 --> 00:00:57,721
I just wanna be part of the conversation.

20
00:00:58,475 --> 00:00:59,645
(Penny(arriving with a man in tow):)Hi, guys.

21
00:00:59,809 --> 00:01:02,019
(Penny(arriving with a man in tow):)Looks like you've been
to the Renaissance fair.

